    post47Title: "How Does a Camera Work Without a Lens?",
    post47Excerpt: "A cardboard box with one pinhole makes a real, upside-down, full-color picture. Here is why, and why a smaller hole is sharper but darker.",
    post48Title: "How Do Fiber Optic Cables Work?",
    post48Excerpt: "Light travels in straight lines, so how does it follow a cable across the ocean floor? It does not bend. It gets trapped.",
    post49Title: "How Do Scientists Know What Stars Are Made Of?",
    post49Excerpt: "Nobody has been to a star. We know their ingredients anyway, because every element leaves its own pattern of lines in light.",
    post50Title: "Why Do Things Glow Under a Blacklight?",
    post50Excerpt: "Tonic water and highlighters are not reflecting the lamp. They are absorbing light you cannot see and making new light of their own.",
    post51Title: "Is Light a Wave or a Particle?",
    post51Excerpt: "It interferes like a wave and arrives like a particle. Two centuries of argument, and what you can and cannot see at home.",
