  faqPage: {
    title: "Frequently Asked Questions",
    description: "Everything you need to know about Avanza STEM.",
    stillHaveQuestions: "Still have questions?",
    contactDescription: "Reach out and we'll get back to you as soon as possible.",
    emailUs: "Email Us",
    items: [
      {
        question: "Is Avanza STEM really free?",
        answer: "Yes, completely. Our project guides, blog content, and workshop resources are available online at no cost, and curriculum lessons are launching soon. Our in-person workshops are also free to attend because we believe cost should never be a barrier to STEM education.",
      },
      {
        question: "What ages are your programs designed for?",
        answer: "Our programs are designed for students in 2nd grade and up (roughly ages 7-14). Some workshops are structured for specific grade ranges, which we always list in the event details.",
      },
      {
        question: "Do I need any prior STEM knowledge?",
        answer: "Not at all. Everything we create is beginner-friendly and designed to be a student's first introduction to the topic. We start from the very basics.",
      },
      {
        question: "Where are the workshops held?",
        answer: "We host workshops at local public libraries in New Jersey, and with partner libraries abroad. Past programs have been held at Clifton Public Library, Allwood Branch Library, Library of the Chathams, Roseland Free Public Library, Wayne Public Library, Verona Public Library, and Little Falls Public Library, plus the Wenbo Shuijing Community Reading Room and Lanyu Books in Shanghai. We're always expanding to new locations, so subscribe to our newsletter to stay updated.",
      },
      {
        question: "How can I be notified about upcoming workshops?",
        answer: "Subscribe to our newsletter at the bottom of the Blog page. We announce upcoming events there.",
      },
      {
        question: "Can I use Avanza STEM curricula in my classroom?",
        answer: "Our current project guides and workshop resources are free for educators, and structured curriculum lessons are launching soon. If you'd like to partner or have us run a workshop at your school, reach out at liam@avanzastem.org.",
      },
      {
        question: "What languages are your materials available in?",
        answer: "Our website is fully available in English, Spanish, Simplified Chinese, and Portuguese. You can switch languages using the globe icon in the navigation bar.",
      },
      {
        question: "How can I volunteer or get involved?",
        answer: "We'd love to have you! Volunteers help with tutoring, running workshops, reviewing curriculum, event setup, and community outreach. Commitment is flexible. We work around your schedule. Email liam@avanzastem.org with a bit about yourself and how you'd like to help.",
      },
      {
        question: "Do students need to bring anything to workshops?",
        answer: "No. We provide all materials. Just show up ready to learn and have fun. We do recommend wearing clothes you don't mind getting a little messy during hands-on building activities.",
      },
      {
        question: "How is Avanza STEM funded?",
        answer: "Avanza STEM is a community-supported initiative operating on a small budget. Interested in supporting materials or future workshops? Email liam@avanzastem.org so we can coordinate what is actually needed.",
      },
    ],
  },

