        qA2aText: "It's fine — reusing the data saves time.",
        qA2aExp: "Reusing training data hides whether it really generalizes.",
        qA2bText: "The score may just show memorization, not real learning.",
        qA2bExp: "Correct — test on unseen examples to measure generalization.",
        qA2cText: "The model will run too slowly.",
        qA2cExp: "Speed isn't the issue here.",
        qA2dText: "It needs more categories.",
        qA2dExp: "The issue is the split, not the number of categories.",
        qA3Prompt: "The chatbot answers a family's question with “95% confidence.” What does that confidence mean?",
        qA3Exp: "Confidence compares the model's options; it is not a guarantee the answer is true — a model can be confident and wrong.",
